From e8c4af5ace1fd9f02c6ccfc21c4c0030d6d175b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Memduh=20=C3=87elik?= <memduhcelik33@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 12:41:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: prevent archive downloads from following escape symlinks

ZIP generation used std::fs::metadata(), which follows symlinks, so the
subsequent is_symlink() check never fired and --no-symlinks was a no-op
for ZIP archives. A symlink inside the served tree that pointed outside
could therefore have its target contents packaged into the download.

Detect symlinks via DirEntry::file_type() (which does not follow), skip
them when --no-symlinks is set, and never include targets that resolve
outside the directory being archived for ZIP, TAR, and TAR.GZ.

Walk TAR trees ourselves (with follow_symlinks disabled on the builder)
so the same containment rules apply. Broken/unresolvable links are
omitted instead of aborting the whole archive stream.

Adds regression tests for the #1568 escape-symlink cases, including
with and without --no-symlinks, and keeps following in-root symlinks
when allowed.

Fixes #1568
